# Glean Platform Usage Analytics — Slide Points

---

## Slide 1: Title

- **Glean Platform Usage Analytics**
- May 2026 | Last 7 Days

---

## Slide 2: What Is This Dashboard?

- Built on Kibana to track Glean platform adoption across the org
- Data ingested from Glean API into Elasticsearch via automated Python pipeline
- Covers three key areas: Platform-wide usage, AI Assistant, and Agents
- Enables data-driven decisions on adoption, engagement, and ROI

---

## Slide 3: Platform Overview

- **1,300 monthly active users** across the organization
- **950 weekly active users** with a **72% stickiness ratio** — users keep coming back
- ~47% of employees (2,005 out of 4,229) have signed up
- **14,600+ searches** performed with **71.6% satisfaction**
- Search is the primary use case, but AI features are growing fast
- Daily active user trends show steady engagement with a spike around May 10–11

---

## Slide 4: Assistant Analytics

- **739 monthly active users** — 57% of all platform users engage with the AI assistant
- **70.9% stickiness** — assistant users return just as often as search users
- AI Answers and Summarization are the most-used features
- Chat volume correlates closely with daily active users
- Feedback collection is minimal — need more signal to measure quality

---

## Slide 5: Agents Analytics — Adoption

- **165 monthly active users** using agents — early but growing fast
- **27 agents deployed** across the platform
- **43% stickiness** — lower than platform average, room to build habit
- Agent runs spiked from ~5 to ~60 per day in just one week — momentum is real

---

## Slide 6: Agents Analytics — Who's Using Them?

- **Sales Development leads** with 66 users, 356 runs, and 29.2% adoption rate
- Usage is concentrated in sales-focused teams
- 10 departments have some agent activity, but most are below 10 runs
- Opportunity to expand agents into Ops, Campaign Management, and other teams

---

## Slide 7: Agents Analytics — Top Agents

- **"The Competitive Companion"** is the #1 agent — 87 users, 145 runs, 8 upvotes, zero downvotes
- Top 4 agents drive the majority of all runs
- Most popular agents support competitive intelligence and sales enablement workflows
- Long-tail agents exist but have limited adoption — need promotion or retirement

---

## Slide 8: Key Wins

- 72% stickiness shows the platform is sticky and valuable
- Over half the user base is actively using AI-powered features
- Agents went from near-zero to 60 daily runs in one week
- Sales Development is an organic champion — adopted agents without heavy push
- Dashboard now gives full visibility into platform health

---

## Slide 9: Areas to Improve

- 53% of employees still haven't signed up — big onboarding opportunity
- Search satisfaction at 71.6% — good but not great, need to dig into low-quality queries
- Feedback volume is too low to measure assistant or agent quality reliably
- Agent stickiness at 43% suggests users try once but don't always come back
- Agent usage is heavily concentrated in Sales — need broader department coverage

---

## Slide 10: Next Steps

- Run targeted onboarding campaigns to close the 53% signup gap
- Embed in-flow feedback prompts in assistant and agent responses
- Partner with Sales Development as agent champions to drive org-wide adoption
- Study what makes "The Competitive Companion" successful and replicate the pattern
- Build department-specific agents for Ops and Campaign Management
- Evaluate and retire underperforming long-tail agents
- Establish a monthly reporting cadence from this dashboard

---
